[{:db/id "q-275105/field-1/eee67a4964b086b56275d82712df56d56a42bbbb09fd4cbfc01d1b8eba5e699e" :answer/id #uuid "e3175648-7718-5eeb-a2a8-de33dc893e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3x^2-9x+30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275105/field-1/2316828e62234c6c64f1bbe7f5b709b1eed313ba45c5354e32ca77bda0980271" :answer/id #uuid "d513065d-9c14-5425-aeea-3995ee21b69d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3x^2+9x+30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275105/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfec8835-f216-5930-b0de-838ed3570de5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275105/field-1/eee67a4964b086b56275d82712df56d56a42bbbb09fd4cbfc01d1b8eba5e699e" :answer-field/choices ["q-275105/field-1/eee67a4964b086b56275d82712df56d56a42bbbb09fd4cbfc01d1b8eba5e699e" "q-275105/field-1/2316828e62234c6c64f1bbe7f5b709b1eed313ba45c5354e32ca77bda0980271"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275105" :question/id #uuid "77ae731a-e7b1-5d7d-a016-3032b69c72a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-275105" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2,{x}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-3.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(-3)(x-2)(x-(-5)) \\\\  & =-3(x-2)(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3(x-2)(x+5) & =-3({x}^{2}+5x-2x-10) \\\\  & =-3({x}^{2}+3x-10) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275105/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-282069/field-1/1931d0c85271d34ed40f28a4c311a4c0a18f49a623997f768b1ce719cbe20ac3" :answer/id #uuid "01414e6a-64f6-51e7-910e-a137c6e15089" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^2+x-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282069/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d714f5f-e8eb-584f-b65f-5aff335e240b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282069/field-1/1931d0c85271d34ed40f28a4c311a4c0a18f49a623997f768b1ce719cbe20ac3" :answer-field/choices ["q-282069/field-1/1931d0c85271d34ed40f28a4c311a4c0a18f49a623997f768b1ce719cbe20ac3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282069" :question/id #uuid "82ac93a9-a71e-5418-8ea8-2d2c10682648" :question/math-academy-id "q-282069" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(1)(x-(-5))(x-4) \\\\  & =(x+5)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)(x-4) & ={x}^{2}-4x+5x-20 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{2}+x-20.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-282069/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-46582/selection/a4d33943d7f1d84455041d18698e696f626a6eee720fcd1a53a45fb13f3fb2fe" :answer/id #uuid "29406218-a3ab-5a3d-aa31-86d7be8fa8d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{t}^{2}+100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-46582/selection/a9ec4